# Feature documentation

When adding **new functionality** to this application (new pages, services,
workflows, admin tools, integrations, or user-visible behavior changes), create
**two documents before or alongside implementation**:

## 1. Planning document

- **Location:** `NMSFM_FGF_CVE/NMSFMFireGrantWF/docs/planning/`
- **Filename:** `<feature-slug>-plan.md` (kebab-case, e.g. `manage-agency-information-plan.md`)
- **Purpose:** High-level plan for stakeholders — problem, decisions, scope, phases,
  success criteria, out-of-scope, rollback.
- **Link** to the detailed implementation doc at the top.

## 2. Implementation document

- **Location:** `NMSFM_FGF_CVE/NMSFMFireGrantWF/docs/`
- **Filename:** `<feature-slug>-implementation-plan.md`
- **Purpose:** Developer-ready spec — architecture, file-by-file changes, service
  signatures, UI/code-behind steps, constants, QA checklist, build command.
- **Link** back to the planning doc.

## Agent behavior

- Create or update both docs when starting a new feature; do not skip for "small"
  features if they add new user-facing or admin behavior.
- Keep planning docs concise; put step-by-step implementation detail in the
  implementation doc.
- Match existing doc headers: Project, Document version, Date, Status, Related
  artifacts.
- After implementation, update **Status** in both docs (Planned → Implemented).

## Exemptions

- Bug fixes with no behavior change
- Dependency/CVE-only updates
- Typo or comment-only edits
